From 518d1af4bdbbd8d95b47a35e36cc0e1e3e487054 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:03:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cli): camcraft-cli mcp, a stdio MCP server that drives a
 headless job

An AI agent (any MCP client) can now program a part step by step over
JSON-RPC 2.0 on stdio, per the public MCP spec (2025-06-18; 2025-03-26 and
2024-11-05 negotiated): initialize, ping, tools/list, tools/call.

Tools (17): open_project, save_project, import_model, get_job,
list_operation_types, list_tool_catalog, add_tool, set_stock,
add_operation, edit_operation, delete_operation, set_tool, undo, redo,
generate, verify, post. Each has a JSON input schema; unknown arguments
are refused.

- One session is one script::Env (document + History). The load, save,
  import, generate, verify and post verbs are the job-script host's,
  called directly, so all three lanes share one meaning per verb.
- Every write is a real command through the History (AddTool, SetStock,
  CreateOperation, EditOperationParams, EditOperationLinks,
  DeleteOperation, ImportModel, GenerateOperation), so undo/redo walk it.
- Params use the project file's DTO shape (new project/json.rs).
  edit_operation is a JSON merge patch over the kind's fields; a field
  the kind lacks is refused by name.
- verify adds structured findings: op, move index, kind, message,
  blocks_post, plus the post gate's problems.
- Every refusal is an MCP tool error (isError), including an unknown
  tool. Protocol junk gets JSON-RPC errors. tools/call has a
  catch_unwind backstop. No unwrap, expect or panic on any path.
- serde_json only; no MCP SDK (rmcp would pull in tokio). Design is in
  RECOMMENDED.md.

Pinned by tests/mcp.rs: handshake_and_tool_list,
a_whole_job_over_the_tools, bad_input_is_a_tool_error_never_a_panic,
the_stdio_loop_answers_line_for_line.

Owed: #180 face/edge/loop picks, #181 WCS/machine/fixtures,
#182 sim render, #183 GUI server mode.

Refs #128

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
